# How git stores and checks out files, the same on every operating system.

# Text files use LF line endings in the repository and in your working copy, so
# diffs never show line-ending noise (Windows editors handle LF fine).
* text=auto eol=lf

# CSV files keep their bytes exactly as they are. The sample data uses CRLF line
# endings, as the CSV standard (RFC 4180) and Excel exports do, which also tests
# that the app reads them correctly.
*.csv -text

# uv writes this file. GitHub folds generated files in pull request diffs.
backend/uv.lock linguist-generated=true
